Z||000000||chris6878||12-19-1999||05:13 PM||||My back manifold is leaking and my car is loud...   i am looking for a replacement manifold now... and was wondering if that plate that goes between the manifold and the block is neccesary..    I have it on the car now, but may take it off when i change the cracked manifold.  <P>thanks for any help..<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||12-19-1999||05:17 PM||||put it back on. It serves as a heat shield and oil deflector.<P>it helps keep the valve cover cooler. should the valve cover leak, wich it will at some point, it keeps oil away from the manifold.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-19-1999||09:22 PM||||Just have your manifold welded no need to get a "new" one. Best pull the other one too as it will soon crack plus it gives you an excuse to do the restriction removal thing||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||12-20-1999||07:05 PM||||That piece of sheetmetal is part of a recall.  It comes in a kit form that includes the manifold, bolts gasket, and some big tube they didn't know what to do with.  The kit for about the same price as the manifold itself.  My Fiero is my only car and being grounded is not an option right now or I would have taken the time to remove the restrictor plates &gt; <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.  The kit resales for about 170.00 here in Monterey CA.. I'm not sure what the retail price would be(230.00?).  Just another option if you don't have the time to play.||||reg||1
